    "result_text": "Done. The build and the full test suite (`AcceptanceTest`, the only test class) are green.\n\n## What I implemented\n\n`riskFlag` is now returned on the owner response, computed as the OR of three soft conditions \u2014 matching the spec exactly. The logic reuses the existing helpers so it stays consistent with the flags already surfaced elsewhere:\n\n- **New `RiskFlag.of(owner, repo)`** (`rest/function/owner/RiskFlag.java`) returns `true` when any of:\n  - the owner is a **possible duplicate** \u2014 `PossibleDuplicate.matchFor(...) != null` (same existing signal as `possibleDuplicate`);\n  - the email domain is **disposable-adjacent** \u2014 `DisposableEmail.isAdjacent(email)`;\n  - the city is **over its soft capacity** \u2014 `CityCapacity.warningFor(...)` (the existing `capacityWarning` threshold).\n\n- **New `DisposableEmail` helper** centralizes the disposable-domain blocklist (previously inline in `ValidateOwner`, which I refactored to call `DisposableEmail.isBlocked`). \"Adjacent\" means a domain that isn't itself blocked but shares a blocked provider's second-level label \u2014 e.g. `inbox.mailinator.com` (subdomain) or `mailinator.net` (same name, different TLD). These slip past the exact-match create-time block yet still read as disposable, so they raise the flag.\n\n- **Wiring:** added `riskFlag` to `openapi.yml` (so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the property), marked it `ignore` in `OwnerMapper`, and set it in all three places that build a single-owner DTO: `RespondWithOwner` (GET), `RespondWithOwnerCreated` (POST), and `CheckIdempotencyKey` (idempotent replay) \u2014 so the flag is consistent across every path that returns an owner.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreRiskFlagFalseNormally`) passes: a fully-unique owner with no email, a unique city, and a distinct surname trips none of the three conditions, so `riskFlag` is `false`.",
